#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-server-mode: Server mode (docs/SERVER-MODE.md), the third mode next to Steam Game Mode and Desktop Mode. The
session (nimbus-session run_server) starts a small labwc with one full-screen dashboard (server-mode.qml, next to this
file); the home server's services keep running as their own units underneath, and this helper only shows and controls
them. Off until you turn it on (Settings › Home server › Server mode); every failure ends in Game Mode.

  hearth-server-mode status              JSON for Settings: your Server mode choices (defaults filled in), the
                                         Start in mode, the PIN set or not, the web page's address
  hearth-server-mode set KEY VALUE       on, idlePower, webOn, permServices, permModes, permPower, permDevices,
                                         scheduleOn (on|off); gpuWatts (80|100|120|150|200); idleMinutes (5|10|20|30);
                                         dim (0|1|2|5|10 minutes); off (0|5|10|20|30|60 minutes)
  hearth-server-mode schedule-set        JSON on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT) {"weekday": [{"at": "HH:MM", "mode": "server"|
                                         "game"|"desktop"}, ...], "weekend": [...]}: 1-8 changes a day
  hearth-server-mode pin-set             the web page's PIN on stdin (4-12 digits); only its hash is kept
  hearth-server-mode pin-clear           no PIN (the web page then lets nobody in)
  hearth-server-mode start-in [MODE]     print, or set (game|desktop|server), what the PC starts in (session.conf's
                                         NIMBUS_START_MODE, through hearth_settings_io: only that line changes)
  hearth-server-mode session-check       "on" when Server mode is on (nimbus-session)
  hearth-server-mode start-mode MODE     the mode the session starts in: MODE, or the schedule's when it's on
  hearth-server-mode dash                JSON for the dashboard
  hearth-server-mode summary             the dashboard in short (Quick Access, Hearth Link, the web page)
  hearth-server-mode back                once after you come back from Game Mode: how long you played
  hearth-server-mode go MODE             switch now (game|desktop|server|logout): the dashboard, after its countdown
  hearth-server-mode request             JSON on stdin: ask the agent ({"kind": "mode", "to"} | {"kind": "power",
                                         "what": "sleep"|"restart"} | {"kind": "service", "name", "action"})
  hearth-server-mode countdown | cancel  the countdown on the home screen (a switch asked for from the web page or the
                                         schedule), or cancel it
  hearth-server-mode service ACTION NAME restart|pause|resume one service: ai, pictures, voices, media, aishare, remote
  hearth-server-mode power sleep|restart|off
  hearth-server-mode idle-power on|off   lower power limits while nothing is busy, or back to how they were
  hearth-server-mode leaving             the session: Server mode ended (power limits back to how they were)
  hearth-server-mode nudge [--wait-game] the services timer's run now, so Light mode pauses / resumes right away
  hearth-server-mode agent               the session's helper: the web page's requests, countdown deadlines, the
                                         schedule (one at a time; ends when Server mode and the web page are off)
  hearth-server-mode serve               the web page (hearth-server-mode-web.service, port 8460)
  hearth-server-mode web-apply           the web page's user service on or off to match your choices
  hearth-server-mode sleep-idle          "on" when you chose Sleep after idle (the session then doesn't hold sleep off)
  hearth-server-mode ai-unload           AI chat's models out of memory now (hearth-home-server ai-unload)

Your choices: ~/.config/nimbus/server-mode.json through hearth_settings_io (only the key you change; atomic, .bak, merged
under the lock; defaults are filled in when read and never saved). What pauses while you play is Light mode's
(home-server.json, hearth-home-server), never a copy. State, never settings: the PIN's hash and the web page's sign-ins
(~/.local/state/nimbus/server-mode-web.json, 0600), and the runtime folder $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hearth-server (requests,
the countdown, what idle power changed). Nothing here goes through a shell. Output: one JSON line; failures print
"error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
